---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { LEGAL, SITE } from '../config';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy policy" description="Privacy policy (Datenschutzerklärung) for bruchner.dev.">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy policy / Datenschutzerklärung</h1>

    <section aria-labelledby="controller">
      <h2 id="controller">Controller</h2>
      <address>
        {LEGAL.name}<br />
        {LEGAL.street}<br />
        {LEGAL.city}<br />
        {LEGAL.country}<br />
        E-mail: {SITE.email}
      </address>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="summary">
      <h2 id="summary">In short</h2>
      <p>
        This site uses no cookies, no analytics, no tracking and no third-party content. Fonts and all
        other resources are served from this server. Personal data is only processed where this is
        technically necessary to deliver the site, or when you contact me.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="hosting">
      <h2 id="hosting">Hosting and server access</h2>
      <p>
        When you open a page, your browser sends technical data to the server, in particular your IP
        address, the requested URL, date and time, and your browser's user agent. This is necessary to
        deliver the page and protect the server (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). The server does not keep access
        logs of this data.
      </p>
      <p>
        The server is operated by {LEGAL.hostingProvider}, which processes this data on my behalf under
        a data processing agreement (Art. 28 GDPR).
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="storage">
      <h2 id="storage">Local storage</h2>
      <p>
        If you switch between light and dark mode, your choice is saved in your browser's local
        storage. It never leaves your device and you can delete it at any time in your browser settings.
        This storage is strictly necessary for the function you requested (§ 25 Abs. 2 Nr. 2 TDDDG).
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="email">
      <h2 id="email">Contact by e-mail</h2>
      <p>
        If you e-mail me, I process your address and message to answer your enquiry (Art. 6(1)(b) or (f)
        GDPR) and delete them once they are no longer needed, unless statutory retention periods apply.
        E-mail is hosted by Proton AG, Route de la Galaise 32, 1228 Plan-les-Ouates, Switzerland, under a
        data processing agreement. Switzerland has an adequacy decision from the European Commission
        (Art. 45 GDPR).
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="rights">
      <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You have the right to access (Art. 15 GDPR), rectification (Art. 16), erasure (Art. 17),
        restriction of processing (Art. 18), data portability (Art. 20) and to object to processing
        based on legitimate interests (Art. 21). To exercise them, e-mail {SITE.email}.
      </p>
      <p>
        You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR), for
        example the Bayerisches Landesamt für Datenschutzaufsicht, Promenade 18, 91522 Ansbach.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
